It's implied that he was also having to do
terrible things while he was with them

00:11:39.632 --> 00:11:41.300
because the whole idea
is that the fireflies,

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:44.336
even though they seem
like a really good group, do things

00:11:44.336 --> 00:11:47.606
that are just as bad as Phaedra
and as the Hunters.

00:11:47.606 --> 00:11:50.242
Morally speaking,
pretty much everyone on the show are just

00:11:50.242 --> 00:11:53.746
shades of gray
like no one is truly good or truly evil.

00:11:53.746 --> 00:11:57.183
Eventually, Tommy leaves the fireflies,
and that's where Joel lost

00:11:57.183 --> 00:12:01.087
contact with him and why he's going to
Wyoming to find out what happened to him.

00:12:01.087 --> 00:12:04.056
His whole conversation with Ellie
about what really matters in life,

00:12:04.056 --> 00:12:05.825
why it's important to continue living

00:12:05.825 --> 00:12:09.228
is also really important
for their whole arc in the series.

00:12:09.228 --> 00:12:10.362
Just in general.

00:12:10.362 --> 00:12:13.399
More specifically, it foreshadows
some of the controversial decisions

00:12:13.399 --> 00:12:16.402
that Joel will make regarding
Ellie towards the end of the first game.

00:12:16.402 --> 00:12:18.237
It will probably be the end of season one,

00:12:18.237 --> 00:12:22.007
like I believe they're meant to cover
all the first game during season one,

00:12:22.007 --> 00:12:26.345
when he eventually does start to think of
her as family, as his surrogate daughter.

00:12:26.345 --> 00:12:28.214
Like in this conversation,
he's loving Ellie.

00:12:28.214 --> 00:12:29.515
No, in no uncertain terms,

00:12:29.515 --> 00:12:32.351
family is the most important thing,
more important

00:12:32.351 --> 00:12:34.987
than anything more important
than the rest of the human race.

00:12:34.987 --> 00:12:36.856
So remember that
it's like the core of his being.

00:12:36.856 --> 00:12:40.459
It informs every decision
that he makes, even all the terrible stuff

00:12:40.459 --> 00:12:43.662
he was forced to do while he was still
with the hunters a long time ago.

00:12:43.662 --> 00:12:47.299
He was doing it in the name
of keeping his family Tommy, safe.

00:12:47.299 --> 00:12:49.602
Right now, Ellie,
who just barely experienced all this,

00:12:49.602 --> 00:12:51.871
she's so young, is looking for a reason
to continue.

00:12:51.871 --> 00:12:54.774
Like, what is the point of living
if it's going to be like this?

00:12:54.774 --> 00:12:57.543
And Joel's just telling him,
you continue because of family.

00:12:57.543 --> 00:12:59.812
I'm sure there's a fast
and Furious meme in here somewhere.

00:12:59.812 --> 00:13:03.182
Like Joel will eventually say
the word family almost as many times

00:13:03.182 --> 00:13:06.485
as Vin Diesel says the word family
when they encounter the roadblock.

00:13:06.485 --> 00:13:08.888
All this is generally
the same as the game.

00:13:08.888 --> 00:13:12.625
But they made the big change from
Pittsburgh to Kansas City in the episode.

00:13:12.625 --> 00:13:14.760
The hunters are meant to be
a rogue faction in the game,

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:18.030
like the fireflies, who seek to establish
their own dominance over Phaedra.

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:20.533
The hunters
also want to get rid of Phaedra as well,

00:13:20.533 --> 00:13:24.136
but they have their own idea
of what order is in the apocalypse.

00:13:24.136 --> 00:13:27.072
Within the context of the story,
the hunters overthrew

00:13:27.072 --> 00:13:30.643
the federal authority in Kansas City,
in Pittsburgh, in the game,

00:13:30.643 --> 00:13:33.612
and just continued to rule the city
with an iron fist,

00:13:33.612 --> 00:13:36.916
killing outsiders
that would come along for their supplies.

00:13:36.916 --> 00:13:38.384
They set up this massive roadblock

00:13:38.384 --> 00:13:41.387
here at the tunnel as an elaborate trap,
forcing outsiders

00:13:41.387 --> 00:13:44.490
to enter the city where it be easier
to kill them and take their stuff.

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:48.961
They had these roadblocks in all
the entrances and exits to the city.

00:13:48.961 --> 00:13:52.198
That's why when they're entering the city,
the camera pans across that burned

00:13:52.198 --> 00:13:53.332
pile of skeletons.

00:13:53.332 --> 00:13:56.769
Those are bodies of regular people
not infected that the hunters

00:13:56.769 --> 00:14:00.206
had previously killed,
like they tried to do to Joel in a year,

00:14:00.206 --> 00:14:01.740
the scene of the hunter
pretending to be hurt

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:03.609
to get them out of the car is right
out of the game.

00:14:03.609 --> 00:14:07.446
The reason why Joel knows immediately
there's that trap is because he was

00:14:07.446 --> 00:14:10.683
one of them and would have done
the exact same thing in this situation.

00:14:10.683 --> 00:14:13.319
Going to help him?
Put your seatbelt on, Ellie,

00:14:14.386 --> 00:14:15.721
what about the guy?

00:14:15.721 --> 00:14:16.922
He ain't even hurt.

00:14:16.922 --> 00:14:19.491
They're only a couple of hunters
that they deal with at this trap here.

00:14:19.491 --> 00:14:21.694
But they have traps
like this all over the city.

00:14:21.694 --> 00:14:23.662
Their group is relatively large.

00:14:23.662 --> 00:14:27.967
It's meant to show you how they control
all access in and out of the city.

00:14:27.967 --> 00:14:30.102
They're all mission here is to escape
the city.

00:14:30.102 --> 00:14:31.170
They're going to have to do this

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:34.540
again, like escape through
another group of hunters to get out.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:37.243
This whole encounter here
is meant to be more about Ellie, though.

00:14:37.243 --> 00:14:40.412
Saving Joel and using Bill's gun
in proving to Joel

00:14:40.412 --> 00:14:41.647
that she herself could do it

00:14:41.647 --> 00:14:45.985
once she was capable of being useful
and who she also deserved to have a gun.

00:14:45.985 --> 00:14:48.721
She almost enjoys this moment here, too,
pulling the trigger.

00:14:48.721 --> 00:14:49.288
But that's

00:14:49.288 --> 00:14:52.825
when the hunters back was turned,
when she didn't have to face him directly.

00:14:52.825 --> 00:14:55.461
You can see her moment of hesitation
when he turns around and starts

00:14:55.461 --> 00:14:58.197
to sob story
to get her to stop. When she talked

00:14:58.197 --> 00:15:00.833
about having to kill someone
before like this isn't her first time.

00:15:00.833 --> 00:15:03.369
That time was also very different
from what's happening here.

00:15:03.369 --> 00:15:06.238
It was still super traumatic,
but she absolutely had to do it.

00:15:06.238 --> 00:15:08.240
It was sort of a fight
or flight kind of thing.

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:10.075
This time, she's in
no immediate danger. It's

00:15:10.075 --> 00:15:13.846
more her killing someone in cold blood,
which she talks to Joel about later.

00:15:13.846 --> 00:15:16.982
She isn't able to kill someone in cold
blood yet.

00:15:16.982 --> 00:15:18.684
That's also a big part of her art, too,

00:15:18.684 --> 00:15:21.687
like the way that she just deals
with surviving in the apocalypse.

00:15:21.687 --> 00:15:24.957
Like the terrible things
that you have to do in order to survive.

00:15:24.957 --> 00:15:27.860
Joel on the other hand,
obviously, no problem killing people

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:31.563
for any reason, even though in this case
it's totally warranted like that.

00:15:31.563 --> 00:15:33.866
Hunter definitely would have either
informed on them

00:15:33.899 --> 00:15:36.936
or continued to try and kill Joel
and Ellie after the fact.

00:15:36.936 --> 00:15:37.903
The reason that he uses

00:15:37.903 --> 00:15:41.006
the Hunter's knife to finish
the job is just pure resource management.

00:15:41.006 --> 00:15:42.541
As Bill said in episode three, it's

00:15:42.541 --> 00:15:45.044
all about resource management
in the apocalypse.

00:15:45.044 --> 00:15:46.512
Conserve your bullets.

00:15:46.512 --> 00:15:48.213
Also, knives make way less noise

00:15:48.213 --> 00:15:51.050
and they really want to avoid
alerting more hunters

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:52.785
when they're escaping
to the other building.

00:15:52.785 --> 00:15:55.054
The Humvee that passes by is one
the hunters stole

00:15:55.054 --> 00:15:57.189
from the federal authority
during the uprising.

00:15:57.189 --> 00:15:58.924
The other cars,
they just scavenge from what

00:15:58.924 --> 00:16:00.459
they could put together across the city

00:16:00.459 --> 00:16:04.863
and other supplies that they've stolen
from unsuspecting travelers.

00:16:04.863 --> 00:16:07.132
We meet Melanie Lynskey,
Kathleen character.

00:16:07.132 --> 00:16:08.100
She's not from the game.

00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:09.902
She's like a brand new character
